    "_%n post in the last twelve weeks_::_%n posts in the last twelve weeks_" : ["%n cummentu in is ùrtimas dòighi chidas","%n cummentos in is ùrtimas dòighi chidas"],
    "_{count} post_::_{count} posts_" : ["{count} cummentu","{count} cummentos"],
    "_{count} following_::_{count} following_" : ["{count} sighidu","{count} sighidos"],
    "_{count} follower_::_{count} followers_" : ["{count} sighidore","{count} sighidores"],
    "A <link rel=\"me\"> in the page's <head> does the same, and rel=\"me noopener\" counts as well: the server looks for \"me\" among the rel words of any anchor or link on the page. The address has to be your own profile address, the one in the line above; a trailing slash or a #fragment makes no difference." : "Unu <link rel=\"me\"> in s'<head> de sa pàgina faghet su matessi, e fintzas rel=\"me noopener\" contat: su serbidore chircat \"me\" tra is faeddos rel de cale si siat àncora o ligòngiu de sa pàgina. S'indiritzu depet èssere s'indiritzu de su profilu tuo, cussu de sa riga de subra; un'istanga a s'acabbu o unu #frammentu non faghent diferèntzia.",
    "This server fetches the page itself, in the background, at most once a day per account, over http or https only, and reads the first part of it. A page it cannot reach is left unverified and asked again later, and a page that stops linking back loses its tick." : "Custu serbidore recùperat sa pàgina a sa sola, in segundu pianu, comente màssimu una borta a sa die pro contu, isceti in http o https, e nde leghet sa prima parte. Una pàgina chi non podet cuntatare abarrat non verificada e est pedida torra prus a tardu, e una pàgina chi tzessat de torrare a ligare perdet su sinnu suo.",
    "{used} of {max} fields used. Remove one, or empty the pronouns or the support link, to save." : "{used} campos impreados de {max}. Nde boga unu, o isbòida is pronùmenes o su ligòngiu de suportu, pro sarvare.",
    "{used} of {max} fields used" : "{used} campos impreados de {max}",
